  "notes": {
    "continentalBoundaries": "Europe/Asia: Urals, Ural River, Caspian Sea, Greater Caucasus watershed, Black Sea and Turkish straits. Africa/Asia: Suez. North/South America: Panama/Colombia boundary. Asia/Oceania: New Guinea belongs to Oceania; the rest of Indonesia is grouped with Asia.",
    "islands": "Caribbean islands and Clipperton are grouped with North America; Madeira and the Canary Islands with Africa; Azores with Europe; Pacific island groups with Oceania. Subantarctic islands are grouped with Antarctica for discovery; this does not put them inside the Antarctic Treaty area.",
    "scope": "FRA and PRT use their approved core geography. ATF spans tropical African islands and subantarctic groups; UMI spans Navassa in the Caribbean and Pacific groups. Neither inherits the continent of its administering country.",
    "transcontinental": "Russia, Turkey, Kazakhstan, Georgia and Azerbaijan cross the documented Europe/Asia divide. Egypt includes Sinai; Indonesia includes western New Guinea; USA includes Hawaii; Chile includes Rapa Nui; Spain includes its African geography."
  },
  "references": [
